      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g per day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g per day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g. A single 5000 mg dose is also well above the usual 1000 mg maximum per dose. At 15 g/day, the risk of serious liver injury is high, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth three times daily (about 2 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day), which is within the limit for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 5000 mg TID, please confirm. I'd still strongly suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
