     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g per day, which is about 3.5 times the maximum daily dose. Doses at that level can cause acute liver failure and death. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't make it safe. I also don't know of any indication that calls for this dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g/day), or 650 mg every 6 hours. Tell me which you want.\n- **Help you check the intent.** If this came from a protocol, a consultant's recommendation, or a transcription from another order, it may contain a unit or decimal error. Pharmacy or your attending can confirm.\n- **Add a note to an order.** If you're treating an acetaminophen overdose, the treatment is acetylcysteine, dosed by weight and level. I can enter that if you give me the details.\n\nIf there's a clinical context I'm missing, tell me and we can go from there."
      }
     ],
